## Post V&V Fallback Boundary Fix

Initial implementation risk: lazy Post V&V fallback could return accepted-like VV reports when real Post V&V import was unavailable.

This was fixed before runtime commit closure.

Fallback Post V&V now fails closed as review-required / needs-revision, not accepted authority. Fallback reports are shape-compatible only; they do not create acceptance, FinalOutput, action permission, or child authority.

Required reason codes:

- post_vv_runtime_unavailable_review_required
- post_vv_fallback_not_authority
- child_output_requires_real_post_vv_or_root_review
- post_vv_fallback_used_review_required

Counter:

- post_vv_fallback_used_count

Forced fallback test exists and passes. Normal real Post V&V path test exists and passes.

## Target Boundary / Child Boundary Fix

It is not enough to check what a child actor outputs; the system must check where child output is being sent.

Dangerous child transitions are blocked:

- child Architect PlanGraph -> final_output
- child Executor ResultProposal -> final_output
- child Verifier VVReport -> final_output
- child GTReport -> final_output
- child GTReport -> parent Architect command
- child Root return -> user FinalOutput

Required reason:

- child_target_boundary_blocked

Canonical child path remains bounded:

- Parent Root / Orchestrator
- Root-shaped task / route
- Fractal Cell boundary
- bounded child actor chain
- child ResultProposal / cell report
- parent Post V&V / GT route
- parent Root final review

